Share native members through lazy tree mappings

Native transport should preserve shared relation subtrees when member
images follow an increasing partial map. Carry compressed offset runs
through both prefix keys and suffix values, caching transformed children
only when needed. Keep general non-injective maps eager and merge their
colliding images into owned destination suffixes.

Preserve canonical current rows, historical snapshots, and finite fuel
through equality and updates. Keep cache lookups in their original key
coordinates, seek directly through partial mapping domains, and resolve
and release deep mapping chains without recursive stack growth.

Bound eager mapping by both prefix width and total materialized work so
small and sparse relations avoid deferred caches. Reject existing lazy
children during preflight without evaluating their callbacks. Represent
dense leaf sets as shared intervals and retain persistent interval trees
when equality introduces many holes.

Keep ordinary nodes compact, update only edited paths, and build sorted
levels without repeated searches. Preserve subtree sharing in unions,
intersections, and differences. Avoid copying removal pivots that are
immediately consumed, and use consistent subtree weights for balancing
and joining. Keep deferred traversal outside ordinary iterator and
update paths so full tuple consumption retains a small hot loop.

Reuse target coverage during ownership cleanup and share transport map
deltas only when both current and previous snapshots match. Distinct
column histories remain independent even when their current maps agree.

Validation includes the full workspace suite, native and desugared
member evaluators under both evaluation strategies, and randomized
mutation sequences checked against an independent relational oracle.
Regression cases cover filtered pivots, partial and conflicting images,
noncanonical rows, source and owner equalities, shared snapshots, long
mapping chains, late images, dynamic roundtrips, and finite fuel.

Compose key-only offset views over their intersecting domains so long
morphism chains need one coordinate translation. Compare the bounded
composed runs exactly to retain cheap equivalent-view comparisons.
Value transforms and fragmented maps preserve their existing paths.

Keep leaf iterator cursors within the element width and expose their
construction to callers so short restrictions avoid unused state.
Preserve the count tag in place during edits and avoid metadata work
when replacing an existing value.

Use exact tree metadata to specialize ordinary insertion and entry
updates. Avoid deferred-node checks and increment unchanged subtree
counts directly; conservative views retain exposure and size repair.
